  "story": {
    "language": "en",
    "translationLanguage": "zh-Hant",
    "textEn": "At school, our teacher asks each group to plan a house that a family will enjoy. We gather around a desk, and every student has a different idea to share. I use a pencil to write our ideas in my notebook while my friend holds up a sheet of paper. We draw the door and window first, then discuss where the family can sit together. A book gives us another idea, and the helpful teacher comes over to listen. Our group is busy, but the students behind us stay quiet so everyone can think. Next, we measure a model with a ruler and compare it with the small model beside it. I move my chair closer so I can see both, and we agree which size will work well. Finally, we show our answer to the teacher and explain how our plan changed.",
    "textZh": "在學校，老師請每個小組設計一間家人會喜歡的房屋。我們圍在書桌旁，每位學生都有不同的想法想分享。我用鉛筆在筆記本裡寫下大家的想法，朋友則舉起一張紙。我們先畫門和窗戶，再討論家人能一起坐在哪裡。一本書給了我們另一個想法，樂於助人的老師也過來聽。我們的小組很忙，後面的學生則保持安靜，讓每個人都能思考。接著我們用尺量一個模型，並拿它和旁邊的小模型比較。我把椅子挪近一點，看清楚兩個模型；我們同意哪個大小合適。最後，我們把答案展示給老師，說明設計如何改變。",
